.TITLE "tail"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays the last part of a file. It outputs the __ending lines__ of text files, making it essential for monitoring log files.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**tail file**
Displays the last ten lines of a file.
> __file__ the target path

**tail -n 20 file**
Displays a specific number of lines from the end of a file.
> __-n__ line count flag | __20__ number of lines

**tail -f file**
Monitors a file in real-time and outputs new lines as they are appended.
> __-f__ follow flag

**tail -c 100 file**
Displays the last specified number of bytes from a file.
> __-c__ byte count flag | __100__ number of bytes

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __tail -f__ command is one of the most useful tools for developers and system administrators to watch log files live. If a file is rotated or replaced, use the __-F__ flag to continue following the new file by name.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:head** **mac:cat**

